[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-16201"] :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -7 & \\le 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 7 \\\\ -7 & \\le x\\le 7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-7\\le x\\le 7.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -3 & \\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 3 \\\\ -3 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-7\\le x\\le 7$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-73602/selection/edcccabd3e36e42b004ebf220cce3463458bb1cca1bf468cb72dde89c55c9763" :answer/id #uuid "832fd3b8-333f-5fb3-a2c1-905dff300675" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/89b88f56878aeb33afe775e083c3775aaa701b6d293ca62e0bd3f2a78923159a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73602/selection/9529ab03e54824746e0b5c4cc65013dfd683430b1e12c1c0907bcbabe37def47" :answer/id #uuid "6a57a0c4-73dc-5959-9e02-ce13094157bb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/0e7f02989d53152d1f2d5247f7f42d579956e49743694229d409cd266ec33e46.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73602/selection/c82522ef78b4bfbe6ba94d5a933